<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19356" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gĕhenna</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέεννα</span> (Hebrew,
		Ge-Hinnom, Ge-Ben-Hinnom), a valley near Jerusalem where children were
		offered to Moloch; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hence, transf.,</span>”
				<i>hell</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Matt. 5, 22 sq.</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">10, 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">18, 9 al.</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 47</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Prud. Cath. 6, 111</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11,
				112</span></i>; Aus. Ephem. ap. Orat. 56 et
			saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gĕhen-nālis</span></b> , e, <i>hellish</i>, <i>of hell</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incendium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Amic. 22, § 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">poenae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 24</span></i>
			, § 4.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
